Generate an Ed25519 identity key (PKCS#8 PEM, mode 0600) and write a
creation-time sidecar at <key>.meta. The last line printed is always:

    pin: <base64>

This is the CONTRACT output: exchange that line with the remote end and
supply it as --pin (client) or --authorized-client (agent).

Running keygen again without --force is idempotent: the existing key is
read and its pin is printed without modifying any file. Use --force to
rotate the key; all remote ends must re-pair with the new pin.

Usage:
  quic-link keygen [flags]

Flags:
      --force[=true|false]   rotate: overwrite an existing key (peers must re-pair)
  -h, --help[=true|false]    help for keygen
      --out string           path to the Ed25519 identity key (PKCS#8 PEM) (default "/home/golden/.config/quic-link/key.pem")

Global Flags:
      --config string      path to config file (optional)
      --log-level string   log verbosity: debug, info, warn, or error (default "info")
